{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>When the ram's horn sounds long, they shall come up to the mountain</b> — this is the shofar of the ram, and it was the shofar of the ram of Isaac (Pirkei deRabbi Eliezer 31). This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 19:13). And I do not understand this, for the ram of Isaac — he offered it as an olah, and the horns and the hooves — all of it is burned in the olot (Zevachim 85b). Perhaps the Holy One, blessed be He, gathered the dust of its horn and restored it to what it had been.\n\nBut in my opinion this aggadah has a sod, and they said that this Voice is the pachad of Isaac, and therefore it says (Exodus 19:16), \"and all the people who were in the camp trembled,\" and they did not attain dibbur in this gevurah except a Voice (Deuteronomy 4:12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "פדר\"א לה resolved as Pirkei deRabbi Elieuter chapter 31. I have left 'pachad of Isaac' and 'gevurah' untranslated where they may carry kabbalistic resonance alongside their plain sense, consistent with the instruction to preserve sod language cryptically; this is a judgment that they function here as quasi-technical terms rather than ordinary words."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:00.747614593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}